  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate Adaptation and Resilience for Communities throug</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This programme aims to strengthen the resilience of poor households in Malawi to withstand current and projected weather and climate-related shocks and stresses. This will in turn halt the annual cycle of humanitarian crises that blights people&#x2019;s lives, harms poverty reduction efforts and swallows up resources. Activities must deliver against FCDO&#x2019;s ICF indicators  1 or  4. Proposals should indicate clearly what other humanitarian/ food insecurity indicators/ resilience indicators they are already using and will continue to use.  
Intervention will be in three districts: Shikwa, Sanje, and Palombe. Please note there is no ToR has been shared and this info based on emails FCDO have sent the humanitarian sub-committee on this opportunity.</narrative>
  </description>
